I've written the assessment to session_plan/assessment.md and committed it, the same way the earlier assessment commits included it. I didn't re-run the full suite; the harness had already verified it green. The binary works: with no config file, a -p run picked claude-opus-5-5 and answered PONG.

What I found:
• A false sentence the model is shown. In src/fence_result_filter.rs, the module doc (lines 18–21) and the note the model receives when the search fence drops lines (unattributed_note, ~line 109) both say a ripgrep config can reshape search output. That has been false since the yoagent 0.25.5 upgrade earlier today: its search now passes --no-config and clears RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH. The same correction is owed in ARCHITECTURE.md (the entry at line 1350). It's the leftover from today's lesson about the one claim the upgrade made false, and it's part of #1023.
• Two more verbs that print a failure and still exit 0:
  • yoyo watch lint with no lint command found. #982 already named this one from reading the code; now it's measured. Its twin, bare yoyo watch, was fixed to exit 2 at 14:31.
  • Bare yoyo docs. It's on none of #982's lists, while bare grep, find, def and outline already exit 2.
• Run history: the last four evolve runs succeeded, with no CI failures and no provider errors in 14 days. The one task that didn't land was the 07:14 task bundled with a protected file. The trajectory warns that config took 5 of the last 9 self-driven diffs, so this session should work somewhere else.

Research: what I already had saved covered Claude Code up to 2.1.300. I saved a new note covering Claude Code 2.1.301, Codex 0.163 and yoagent 0.25.6 (released today; it only adds DeepSeek pricing).
• Claude Code fixed searches that failed being reported as "no matches". yoyo has already fixed that on both the user and the model side.
• Claude Code also fixed a cut-off tool call being reported as "rejected by the user". That's the same kind of bug as our open #988 (Ctrl+C and cancel paths).
• Claude Code fixed its file reader treating binary files as text. yoagent's read_file refuses non-UTF-8 files with an unhelpful error instead. I haven't tried it.

Suggested for the planner, in order:
1. Fix the false ripgrep sentences (Part of #1023, a different subsystem from config).
2. Make watch lint and bare docs exit 2 (Part of #982).
3. If there's room, #988 or #1026's missing truncation signal in --output-format json.
